WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.850
Welcome to Ear Biscuits.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.700
The podcast where two lifelong friends

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:08.450
talk about life for a long time.

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:09.550
I'm Rhett.

00:00:09.550 --> 00:00:10.383
I'm Link.

00:00:10.383 --> 00:00:12.810
This week at the round
table at dim lighting,

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.260
we are fielding your pressing questions

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:20.110
and having what is sure to be
a fun, loving conversation.

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:22.870
Maybe pressing your fielding questions.

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:25.080
Remember Field &amp; Stream, the magazine?

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.420
I remember the cover.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:28.553
It's not like I ever-

00:00:28.553 --> 00:00:29.386
You didn't get it?

00:00:29.386 --> 00:00:30.219
Subscribed to it.

00:00:30.219 --> 00:00:32.760
I for some reason, I
would get it occasionally.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:33.593
Really?

00:00:33.593 --> 00:00:34.820
Yeah.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:38.020
You weren't a subscriber, but
you would randomly get it.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.910
I would buy it off of the shelf.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:42.193
It was also-

00:00:42.193 --> 00:00:43.220
I don't know why because
I was like I like field

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.053
and I like streams.

00:00:44.053 --> 00:00:44.886
It's fishing and hunting.

00:00:44.886 --> 00:00:47.630
Hunting and fishing,
and I did that as a kid.

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:49.960
We're gonna answer questions including,

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:53.330
would we be friends if we met as adults.

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:56.920
How long should you wait before you honk

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:00.350
at someone who's not going in
front of you on a green light.

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.250
Those are two different questions.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:03.783
They're very much related.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:05.640
I don't know how.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:07.030
Is there a magazine that you would pick up

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:07.913
off of the shelf?

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.623
A magazine that I would pick up,

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:14.860
Entertainment Weekly.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:15.750
That was the magazine-

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:16.583
As a child?

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:22.050
As a middle schooler, and
maybe even a high schooler.

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:24.683
My brother subscribe
to Sports Illustrated.

00:01:25.626 --> 00:01:27.560
You're gonna talk about the
swimsuit issue, aren't you?

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:28.650
The swimsuit issue-

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.650
If you bring up Sports Illustrated, I-

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:32.973
Speaking of Field &amp; Stream-

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:37.600
I distinctly remember
you showing up to school.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:38.433
I brought it to school?

00:01:38.433 --> 00:01:39.420
No, you didn't bring it,

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:42.860
but you brought a report
about it, and not for class.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:43.886
Just for me.

00:01:43.886 --> 00:01:45.440
Well, I don't know exactly
what my parents were-

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:48.360
My brother got Sports
Illustrated swimsuit issue.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.586
I don't know what year the
swimsuit issue came out first.

00:01:50.586 --> 00:01:51.490
Well he got all the issues.

00:01:51.490 --> 00:01:52.760
That's only when you talked about.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:56.150
I don't know which one came out first,

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:56.983
but I don't know.

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.360
The first year, the swimsuit issue,

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:01.214
but I guess that's irrelevant.

00:02:01.214 --> 00:02:02.900
When it first came out,
it was illustrated.

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:04.860
All the sports were illustrated-

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.800
Even the swimsuit issue was illustrated,

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:07.740
which just had the same effect.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:10.610
Yeah, it was basically
like a coloring book.

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:14.482
Which we have one of
those now, spoiler alert.

00:02:14.482 --> 00:02:16.090
It's the one which Kathy Ireland on it.

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:19.870
She now sells home goods.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.143
She has a line at Target.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:24.400
The math adds up for that.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:29.400
Man, well, I don't partake of
the swimsuit issue anymore.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.491
You know what I'm saying?

00:02:33.491 --> 00:02:34.470
It's like, I'm aware of it,

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:36.870
in the way that you're
aware of it on the internet,

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:37.860
and you're like, oh-

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.045
It was a big deal.

00:02:39.045 --> 00:02:41.640
This woman is on the front.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.350
Everybody knows who's on the front,

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:45.650
but back in the day it
was like, well, of course,

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:47.150
I'm gonna spend some time on the front,

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:48.650
but I'm going in.

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:50.570
I'm gonna spend way too much time-

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.270
Well, did you take it in secret?

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:56.800
Did Cole know you were
taking it from his room?

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.090
Your parents certainly
didn't know that he had it.

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:03.200
No, they did because my
mom would get the mail.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.830
I think it was... I mean,
again I'm just going off of

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:08.160
pure conjecture at this point,

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:10.760
but my mom is the one
who collected the mail.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:13.770
I think that she may
just made the decision,

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:15.533
well, he subscribes to this.

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:19.040
That doesn't seem like...

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:22.840
Given the environment and
the amount of oversight...

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:24.470
Well, maybe oversight
is not the right word.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.530
It was just a woman in a bikini.

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:29.410
You know what I'm saying, it wasn't porn.

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:33.390
No, but it seemed
scandalous to us to have it.

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:34.980
I wouldn't be caught dead looking at it

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.630
in the aisle or the shortstop.

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:37.780
That'd be embarrassing.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:39.680
Well there's more
embarrassing things than that.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:40.830
Well, certainly,

00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:45.600
but I just think that we
had a little bit too much.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:46.950
I had a little bit too much shame.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:48.690
Still do apparently.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:51.200
Yeah, ding, ding, ding moment.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.840
I'm just kidding.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:53.673
I mean a lot of-

00:03:53.673 --> 00:03:54.506
We've all gotten shame there.

00:03:54.506 --> 00:03:57.230
A lot of them you'd could see

00:03:57.230 --> 00:03:59.570
more than a bathing suit show.

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:01.430
Well, I mean, especially back in the day.

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:02.430
Back in the day.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:04.540
I mean that's like just everybody.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:06.990
Your teacher wears that
kind of bathing suit now.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:09.460
On her TikTok account.

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:12.040
Do teachers have TikTok now?

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:12.980
I don't even wanna know.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:14.733
Yeah, a teacher TikTok.

00:04:14.733 --> 00:04:15.566
It's a whole section.

00:04:15.566 --> 00:04:16.623
Teacher Tok.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:19.270
I took a trip to Joshua Tree.

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:20.900
Look at me, man.

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:24.100
I come back from Zion,
and then weeks later-

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:24.933
Back from the desert.

00:04:24.933 --> 00:04:28.980
Here I am going back to another

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.590
national park desert location.

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:32.890
Did you know that Joshua Tree did not

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:35.150
become a national park until 1994?

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:37.282
Yeah, after the U2 album.

00:04:37.282 --> 00:04:40.501
That's when they sent the
government over the edge.

00:04:40.501 --> 00:04:42.280
Bill Clinton was like,

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:44.970
I've got to get this place taken care of.

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:47.097
We've gotta protect this place.

00:04:47.097 --> 00:04:48.529
We gotta protect this place, we really do.

00:04:48.529 --> 00:04:49.866
I had a conversation with Bono.

00:04:49.866 --> 00:04:52.650
This is how I had a
conversation with Bono.

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:54.500
He finally returned my calls when I said

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:57.720
I was gonna make Joshua
Tree a national park.

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:00.670
He called me back, and
Edge was in the background.

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:03.657
What year was that album released?

00:05:03.657 --> 00:05:04.490
I don't know.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:06.483
I am not a U2 fan, you know that.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:12.570
Our friend, Mike, took
you to a U2 concert.

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:13.403
Yeah.

00:05:13.403 --> 00:05:14.950
I mean, I respect...

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:16.550
You know I say, I respect U2.

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:18.860
We have very similar tastes in music.

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:21.840
I think the reason why we don't like U2,

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.047
or haven't gotten into U2 it's like,

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.940
it's more about us than it is about U2.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:27.773
Really?

00:05:27.773 --> 00:05:29.093
I think, yeah.

00:05:29.093 --> 00:05:31.243
I think it's about U2, it's not about me.

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:34.173
It's a little... Because just like-

00:05:34.173 --> 00:05:36.200
It's a little too rocky for us.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:37.965
A little too rocky.

00:05:37.965 --> 00:05:38.798
A little too rocky, we
like a little more soul.

00:05:38.798 --> 00:05:40.940
Even when it gets pensive,

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:45.637
it's still a little too rocky for us.

00:05:45.637 --> 00:05:46.470
There's something about that.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.210
We never connected with just pure rock.

00:05:48.210 --> 00:05:49.429
Never got into it.

00:05:49.429 --> 00:05:50.970
I always felt like it wasn't for us.

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:52.460
It's like rap, yeah.

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:53.850
Country, yeah.

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:55.624
Soul, yeah.

00:05:55.624 --> 00:06:00.160
Rock, southern rock, yeah, rock...

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:02.409
Classic rock, yeah, but like-

00:06:02.409 --> 00:06:03.242
Some classic rock, yeah, CCR?

00:06:04.284 --> 00:06:07.343
We're getting it out
of U2, so I don't know.

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:10.420
I think there's people who would try to...

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:13.868
I'm pretty sure there's a
Joshua Tree on the album.

00:06:13.868 --> 00:06:14.701
On the cover people will try to find it.

00:06:14.701 --> 00:06:15.670
Yeah, and that's not-

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:19.080
We can't because I mean,
you see one Joshua Tree,

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.300
you've seen them all.

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:22.335
Well they're all different.

00:06:22.335 --> 00:06:24.310
They're just like Netflix, I know.

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:27.000
But it never snows where Joshua Trees are,

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.950
which is a mind-blowing thing.

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:31.020
Also not true, also not
true, I don't think.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:32.960
You can have some snow at Joshua Tree.

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:37.020
It's like a high desert
and a lower desert meet,

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:38.458
and this Joshua Trees have

00:06:38.458 --> 00:06:39.861
Same amount of elevation.

00:06:39.861 --> 00:06:42.090
They're very specific because even

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:45.020
when we would do an
offloading, over landing trip,

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:48.600
like when we went to Death
Valley for those three

00:06:48.600 --> 00:06:49.740
or four nights.

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:54.740
I remember we'd go into this
one valley or crest this hill.

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:56.950
It was only in one place,

00:06:56.950 --> 00:07:00.170
and we were in this expansive valley.

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:04.100
You lose perspective when
you're driving through

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:05.410
Death Valley, about how...

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:06.800
What altitude you're at.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:07.950
What elevation you're at.

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:10.410
You're not flying, but
what elevation you're at.

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:12.220
If you've got a good spoiler.

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:13.770
Sometimes you might think, oh,

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:15.570
we've been in this valley for a long time,

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:19.680
and then you round another
corner and there's just...

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:24.680
It was just an inlet to
a much more huge valley

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:26.440
because everything gets so expansive.

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:29.500
I remember coming around over one ridge,

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:32.150
and all of a sudden it was
just Joshua Trees everywhere.

00:07:32.150 --> 00:07:33.540
We've been driving for a couple of days,

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:34.373
and it was only in this one place.

00:07:34.373 --> 00:07:36.930
It was one altitude,
but Joshua Tree special

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:39.830
because they're so many
there at that particular...

00:07:41.237 --> 00:07:42.510
I keep meaning to say elevation.

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:45.490
Did you go to the...

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:47.740
I can't remember the name of it,

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:51.630
but there's a forest of
a certain type of cactus

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:53.000
that you can walk through.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:53.833
No.

00:07:53.833 --> 00:07:56.500
It's incredibly, densely...

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:59.370
It's the thing that if
you are playing around

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:03.160
and you pushed your friend,

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:04.970
they would get a bunch of needles in them.

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:08.520
You have to watch where
you're walking, but it's just.

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:09.870
Did you go there?

00:08:09.870 --> 00:08:11.202
Yeah, I've been there twice now.

00:08:11.202 --> 00:08:13.709
No, but to this particular
place you're talking about.

00:08:13.709 --> 00:08:16.300
It's one of the stops
off of the main road,

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.440
if you're going through Joshua Tree.

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:19.880
I haven't but that is the thing-

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:21.630
It's called the so-and-so forest,

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:23.030
and it's just these cacti-

00:08:23.030 --> 00:08:24.333
I didn't even see-

00:08:24.333 --> 00:08:25.936
That are like this tall.

00:08:25.936 --> 00:08:27.086
It's pretty remarkable.

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:29.450
You should have told me that a week ago.

00:08:29.450 --> 00:08:32.450
It's the most unlike
the rest of Joshua Tree,

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.606
but it's not as cool as
the rest of Joshua Tree.

00:08:34.606 --> 00:08:35.460
You're not missing much
but it's just unusual.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:37.990
Well, the thing about
Joshua Tree, you're right.

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:41.530
There's basically one paved road

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:44.174
that goes through Joshua Tree.

00:08:44.174 --> 00:08:46.570
There's some offshoots but not many.

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:48.490
It's pretty Disneyesque in that way.

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:50.580
Yeah, and so you'll go to one parking lot,

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:54.000
and then you'll take the loop trail

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:58.515
with whatever rock features
are associated with that.

00:08:58.515 --> 00:08:59.348
Then you get back in the car

00:08:59.348 --> 00:09:01.370
and you'll drive to another place.

00:09:01.370 --> 00:09:02.523
We had the kids.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:07.480
It was just a family excursion,
and we stayed in an Airbnb.

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.360
Too many people for a van.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:10.910
That's a problem I have.

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:14.933
I'm still obsessing about
this van life on Instagram,

00:09:14.933 --> 00:09:19.933
but Insta-cramming my family
into a van is a bit much.

00:09:20.270 --> 00:09:21.550
We have one too many kids.

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:23.930
What about van life meets trailer life?

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:26.730
It's a van and you haul
a trailer and their kids

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:29.803
are in the trailer, a
windowless trailer behind you.

00:09:29.803 --> 00:09:31.603
I mean, Lily's getting to the age,

00:09:32.490 --> 00:09:33.840
she's going off on her own.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:36.863
I'm just thinking that she's
just not part of the equation.

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:39.470
If I were to get one of these vans,

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:41.940
it would be like, take a kid or two.

00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:45.044
Take a wife or two, but
not take everybody at once.

00:09:45.044 --> 00:09:46.201
I get it.

00:09:46.201 --> 00:09:49.660
I mean, I can take Christie
and Jesse is what I'm saying.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:52.310
Well, Jesse likes to do things on her own.

00:09:52.310 --> 00:09:53.503
With me and Christie.

00:09:56.030 --> 00:09:58.020
You're saying, Jesse likes
to do things without you.

00:09:58.020 --> 00:09:59.770
She can do whatever she wants, man.

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:05.010
You know what, we give
each other lots of freedom.

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:07.110
Something about your response

00:10:07.110 --> 00:10:09.430
rings of a reprimand that you've gotten

00:10:09.430 --> 00:10:11.693
from Jessie about something
you've talked about.

00:10:11.693 --> 00:10:12.526
No, I'm just joking.

00:10:12.526 --> 00:10:15.583
I mean, she really,
she went on a solo trip

00:10:15.583 --> 00:10:16.973
that she really enjoyed.

00:10:19.370 --> 00:10:20.480
That's our thing now.

00:10:20.480 --> 00:10:22.670
We just go on separate trips.

00:10:22.670 --> 00:10:23.770
You alternate.

00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:27.260
Whose weekend is it to be
away from the other person?

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:28.340
This was her first too.

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:29.715
Just once.

00:10:29.715 --> 00:10:33.820
Just maybe annual road trip

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:36.080
each person gets there
because I feel like,

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:39.250
if only one person in the couple is on...

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:41.270
In fact, we were asked
this question in the AMA

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:42.883
on the medical society today.

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:48.450
Somebody was asking, how do
I talk my significant other

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:50.610
into me going on a solo trip.

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:52.910
I was like, I didn't
have to worry about that

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:56.500
because Jesse and I were
both making the decision

00:10:56.500 --> 00:11:00.610
to prioritize a solo trip
independently at the same time.

00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:01.900
Yeah, the answer is-

00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:03.332
You gotta both be onboard.

00:11:03.332 --> 00:11:04.480
Get them to go on one first.

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:06.510
They had to see it as not being about them

00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:07.583
but being about you.

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:09.517
The solo trip-

00:11:09.517 --> 00:11:10.350
What do you mean?

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:11.183
The solo trip has nothing to do

00:11:11.183 --> 00:11:12.920
with me getting away from Jessie.

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:15.240
The solo trip has everything to do with me

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:17.900
having time with myself, and
her having time with herself

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:21.060
so we can come back and be
better people in general,

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:23.470
which benefits the other person
and the rest of the family.

00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:25.020
How's that going, by the way?

00:11:26.090 --> 00:11:27.590
The benefiting of the other people?

00:11:27.590 --> 00:11:29.430
No, are you a better person?

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:31.460
Is it worn off?

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:34.591
I would say, I think he take...

00:11:34.591 --> 00:11:35.424
You just Paula Abdul.

00:11:35.424 --> 00:11:36.440
I think I Paula Abdul-ed it.

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:38.413
One step forward two steps back?

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:42.090
I thought it was two steps
forward and one step back.

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:43.000
Did she say two steps...

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:44.370
One step forward and two steps back?

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:46.820
Two steps forward, two steps...

00:11:46.820 --> 00:11:49.193
I think it's two and two now that I-

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:51.540
Well, then what the hell does Paula do?

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:52.860
Opposites attract.

00:11:52.860 --> 00:11:54.258
She's taking two steps forward

00:11:54.258 --> 00:11:55.150
and that person's taking two steps back?

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:57.560
It ain't fiction, it's a natural fact.

00:11:57.560 --> 00:11:58.700
Two step forward-

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:00.000
She wasn't even talking
about the same thing

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.590
that I'm talking about.

00:12:01.590 --> 00:12:03.210
I'm talking about making forward progress

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:05.077
and then regressing, and then being like

00:12:05.077 --> 00:12:08.910
I feel like I'm in a better
place in some respects,

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:10.120
so not like Paula Abdul.

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:11.490
Like a song that I can't come up with

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:13.260
right now in which I...

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:15.650
I'm glad you asked the question

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:19.010
because I talked to my therapist

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:20.783
right when I got back from the trip.

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:27.090
What we talked about was how you take

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:30.410
this moment that you had
and then entering back

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:31.853
into normal life.

00:12:34.010 --> 00:12:36.523
Normal life wants to undo everything.

00:12:37.369 --> 00:12:40.300
It wants to drag you
back into its normalcy,

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:42.930
and your routines, and your habits,

00:12:42.930 --> 00:12:45.493
and the way that you see
the world by default.

00:12:46.730 --> 00:12:50.520
That has been a struggle
because it's been weeks now

00:12:50.520 --> 00:12:51.423
since I got back.

00:12:54.102 --> 00:12:55.200
I expected that.

00:12:55.200 --> 00:12:56.240
I didn't go in thinking

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:58.180
that I was gonna come back a
completely different person.

00:12:58.180 --> 00:13:00.130
I was like, this is
about the journey, man.

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:03.540
It's about incremental change
in the right direction.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:05.360
That's all I can hope for.

00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:06.430
The thing that I did...

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:07.940
I mean, it wasn't a solo trip,

00:13:07.940 --> 00:13:11.430
but the trip with
Christie was very special

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:14.630
when we went to Utah.

00:13:14.630 --> 00:13:18.610
I came back, and I was actually talking

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:20.243
to my therapist about it.

00:13:20.243 --> 00:13:23.940
Then one of the things that he said was,

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:27.250
he suggested that I make up a photo album.

00:13:27.250 --> 00:13:29.520
A scrapbook.

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:33.036
Well, all of my photos
are in Google photos, so.

00:13:33.036 --> 00:13:33.869
Did he use the term scrapbook?

00:13:33.869 --> 00:13:36.030
No, I just put them into...

00:13:36.030 --> 00:13:38.180
You can order a hard or soft bag.

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:39.250
Apple did it first.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:40.083
Always go hard.

00:13:40.083 --> 00:13:42.630
Now Google does it, and I went hard.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:44.120
I surprised Christie with it

00:13:44.120 --> 00:13:46.610
just so we could have something physical

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:48.860
where it's like memorialize the occasion,

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:50.760
and I put some funny captions in there

00:13:51.828 --> 00:13:53.080
like on that one campsite.

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:56.500
It was like, you're selling hotdogs?

00:13:56.500 --> 00:13:57.333
That kind of thing.

00:13:57.333 --> 00:13:58.390
Yeah, that brings back the
right kind of memories.

00:13:58.390 --> 00:14:01.170
I don't think we would
have forgotten that.

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:06.170
A side note, Google photos books suck ass.

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:08.453
Compared to Apple?

00:14:08.453 --> 00:14:10.114
Compared to Apple.

00:14:10.114 --> 00:14:11.770
Next time I would download...

00:14:11.770 --> 00:14:13.900
They altered all of my photos.

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:15.580
They'd tried to enhance them.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:16.413
Google did?

00:14:16.413 --> 00:14:19.930
Yeah, Google's trying
to saturate my photos.

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:22.220
My photos are the way I want my photos.

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:26.180
Don't apply some general
saturation to everything

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:27.590
that you're printing to where it's like-

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:29.180
If anything you need to desaturate.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:30.013
Just leave it.

00:14:30.013 --> 00:14:31.280
I want it.

00:14:31.280 --> 00:14:32.720
I took the picture.

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:35.280
If I wanted to edit it,
I would have done that.

00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:36.493
I'm not a dummy.

00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:39.620
I'm pretty sure that next time

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:41.580
I'm just gonna download
them all from Google

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:44.240
and I'm gonna upload them
to Apple just to do that.

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:45.930
Even though I don't keep my stuff...

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:46.763
I have a Mac.

00:14:46.763 --> 00:14:49.800
I use Google photos.

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:52.001
Now you run into a problem here.

00:14:52.001 --> 00:14:55.800
I'll tell you this one story
from going to Joshua Tree.

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:56.633
We got an Airbnb.

00:14:56.633 --> 00:14:57.753
It was this place.

00:15:00.397 --> 00:15:03.179
It was a 30 minute drive from
the entrance to Joshua Tree

00:15:03.179 --> 00:15:06.870
north of a place called Pioneertown,

00:15:06.870 --> 00:15:09.610
which they film some stuff there.

00:15:09.610 --> 00:15:12.780
They have a makeshift, western town,

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:15.530
and I think Ice Cube
shot a music video there.

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:16.689
How does that add up.

00:15:16.689 --> 00:15:17.683
I don't know.

00:15:18.590 --> 00:15:23.590
Anyway, so we're out there and the booklet

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:25.930
for the Airbnb there
is tell you what to do

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:26.890
and what not to do.

00:15:26.890 --> 00:15:28.680
If you bring a dog, you
better put them on a sheet

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:31.110
on the couch and that stuff.

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:34.832
They said, out of respect
for our neighbors...

00:15:34.832 --> 00:15:39.832
This house was in the middle
of this desert valley.

00:15:40.280 --> 00:15:41.370
We arrived at night,

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:44.130
and I couldn't tell if there
were any other houses around

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:47.530
for reasons I'll get into,
but they weren't that close.

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:48.810
It's like the neighbors weren't that close

00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:50.120
the next morning I could tell.

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:52.520
The reason why is because of
what they said in the booklet,

00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:54.313
out of respect for the neighbors,

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:59.370
only use outside lighting
when absolutely necessary

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:04.250
and then turn off your
lights so that there...

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:07.610
It decreases light pollution
to help us stargaze.

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:10.100
People are out here in the
desert to see the stars.

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:12.700
I'm real tuned into that
ever since the last trip.

00:16:13.870 --> 00:16:15.220
It was a big selling point.

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:16.470
They had a hot tub out there

00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:19.270
in the middle of the backyard just like-

00:16:19.270 --> 00:16:20.103
Nice.

00:16:20.103 --> 00:16:22.090
Then you get in the hot
tub, and you just lean back,

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:24.660
and you look at this expansive sky

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:28.803
and see what I schooled
Lily on was the Milky Way.

00:16:32.324 --> 00:16:35.533
That first night I mean, they
had flashlights so that...

00:16:35.533 --> 00:16:37.330
Because you can't turn the lights off

00:16:37.330 --> 00:16:38.180
once you get in the hot tub.

00:16:38.180 --> 00:16:39.800
You gotta turn them off from the house

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:44.107
and then walk out and try not
to trip on the Joshua Tree

00:16:44.107 --> 00:16:46.820
and the cacti and the rocks and stuff.

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:48.790
You're using your flashlight.

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:49.623
You getting out there.

00:16:49.623 --> 00:16:52.740
We turn off the lights in the hot tub too,

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:55.150
so it's very black.

00:16:55.150 --> 00:16:58.960
We're looking up at the stars,

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:01.040
but we're having a good old time.

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:04.850
All of a sudden, Lando goes, oh.

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:05.683
You're like what?

00:17:05.683 --> 00:17:09.170
He was like, I just tasted something.

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:11.163
It tasted like sausage.

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:16.890
I said, and we all are what
like, we're like, what?

00:17:16.890 --> 00:17:18.808
Lando is the type that I...

00:17:18.808 --> 00:17:21.273
Lando is a very reactionary kid.

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:24.190
Wouldn't you say?

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:25.449
Yes.

00:17:25.449 --> 00:17:29.780
He's particular about things.

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:33.940
He's a bit queer, kinda
like me meaning that he's...

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:36.180
Well, I don't wanna have to
re-explain what that means,

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:38.193
but it just means particular.

00:17:41.010 --> 00:17:45.260
We didn't wanna say, dude,
there is no sausage floating

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:46.860
in this pool.

00:17:46.860 --> 00:17:48.300
Apparently, he had put his mouth down

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:50.430
at the surface level of the water

00:17:50.430 --> 00:17:53.070
and he got something in
his mouth and he said-

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:55.310
I thought he had burped and
was tasting dinner again.

00:17:55.310 --> 00:17:56.387
No, no.

00:17:56.387 --> 00:18:00.820
We had not had sausage that
night, or the day before.

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:02.480
He had put his mouth down at the water

00:18:02.480 --> 00:18:04.080
and gotten something in his mouth

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:07.440
that he said tasted like sausage.

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:08.963
We didn't wanna alarm him.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:14.780
From before I had turned the light off,

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.440
I was the first one
out there with Lincoln,

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:19.040
and Lincoln was like, you
need to get these bugs out

00:18:20.463 --> 00:18:21.680
of the hot tub.

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:22.670
I didn't wanna tell him that...

00:18:22.670 --> 00:18:25.270
I was pretty sure because
I didn't get the bugs out.

00:18:26.298 --> 00:18:27.790
There was only two of them.

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.290
Now there's only one of them

00:18:30.557 --> 00:18:31.390
I didn't wanna tell him.

00:18:31.390 --> 00:18:33.920
Dude, I think you ate a bug or worse.

00:18:33.920 --> 00:18:37.893
I mean, so as far as I
know, as far as he knows,

00:18:39.410 --> 00:18:41.480
he ate a sausage because
the way that he said it,

00:18:41.480 --> 00:18:44.580
he said, I just got something in my mouth.

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:45.530
It tastes like sausage.

00:18:45.530 --> 00:18:47.113
I could tell by the way he said it.

00:18:47.113 --> 00:18:47.946
It was probably a moth.

00:18:47.946 --> 00:18:48.860
That he did eat it.

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:49.970
It was probably a moth, I could imagine.

00:18:49.970 --> 00:18:51.943
He chewed it up, tasted it,

00:18:53.089 --> 00:18:54.988
experienced the sensation of sausage-

00:18:54.988 --> 00:18:56.368
Why would he chew it?

00:18:56.368 --> 00:18:57.440
Then I think, I don't know.

00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:58.893
I think he just got it in his mouth.

00:18:58.893 --> 00:19:01.850
I think it came in with a
gulp of water or something.

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:05.050
Well, I think he swallowed it.

00:19:05.050 --> 00:19:08.750
He was like, he said it
in a way that was like,

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:11.536
I just got something in my
mouth that tasted like sausage.

00:19:11.536 --> 00:19:12.369
Is this sausage water?

00:19:12.369 --> 00:19:14.100
Is there like a sausage
water in this hot tub?

00:19:14.100 --> 00:19:15.810
I'm telling you more than I'm telling him,

00:19:15.810 --> 00:19:18.360
but he ate something that
I'm afraid is not sausage.

00:19:18.360 --> 00:19:19.860
You haven't talked to him about it?

00:19:19.860 --> 00:19:21.110
Even days later?

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:22.970
We would make fun of...

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:26.070
It's like, man, this tastes like sausage

00:19:26.070 --> 00:19:28.383
for a lot of things, for
the rest of the weekend.

00:19:28.383 --> 00:19:29.713
He didn't bit it again.

00:19:29.713 --> 00:19:31.620
Mission accomplished.

00:19:31.620 --> 00:19:35.720
He never freaked out, but I do
not know exactly what he ate.

00:19:35.720 --> 00:19:37.415
It was definitely a bug because I can...

00:19:37.415 --> 00:19:39.723
Having eaten lots of bugs-

00:19:39.723 --> 00:19:41.740
A soggy sausage-like bugs.

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:44.170
I can imagine, especially an uncooked bug.

00:19:44.170 --> 00:19:46.550
At least, I mean, I guess it's parboiled

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:47.550
because it's in the-

00:19:49.077 --> 00:19:50.774
A lot of chemicals in there.

00:19:50.774 --> 00:19:51.607
It's in the hot tub, but I could tell,

00:19:51.607 --> 00:19:53.720
It's got a little spice to it
and you can't quite reconcile,

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:55.120
so you just go with sausage.

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:58.003
I get it.

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:00.300
Well, I'll tell him the
next time I see him.

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:01.490
Oh my God.

00:20:01.490 --> 00:20:03.280
I was just glad he didn't freak out.

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:04.390
Yeah, because if you had to told him

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:06.370
that he just ate a bug, it
may have ruined your night.

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:07.704
Ruin the evening.

00:20:07.704 --> 00:20:09.870
It wouldn't have been
about the stars anymore.

00:20:11.458 --> 00:20:14.400
Sometimes the truth is not worth.

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:16.370
Yeah, I only tell the truth
when it's convenient for me.

00:20:16.370 --> 00:20:20.030
Now, let's answer some of these questions,

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:22.170
but first let's just let you know

00:20:22.170 --> 00:20:24.390
about something that we are
very, very excited about.

00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:25.990
We don't have a copy of it here.

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:29.660
As of the recording,
it's still being printed,

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:30.493
but that's-

00:20:30.493 --> 00:20:31.450
We know what it looks like though.

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:35.260
This is a high quality product.

00:20:35.260 --> 00:20:40.260
It's a coloring book for
adults and adult children.

00:20:41.140 --> 00:20:43.370
If you've been paying
attention to just the evolution

00:20:43.370 --> 00:20:45.530
of culture over the past decade or so-

00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:46.363
Everybody colors.

00:20:46.363 --> 00:20:47.196
Everybody's coloring now.

00:20:47.196 --> 00:20:49.010
You don't have to be a child anymore.

00:20:50.362 --> 00:20:53.857
We have basically taken
the world of mythicality

00:20:53.857 --> 00:20:55.690
and some of your favorite things

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:58.520
that you have experienced
through the world of mythicality,

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:00.160
and translated them into these

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:03.940
incredibly intricate illustrations

00:21:03.940 --> 00:21:06.250
that then you can colorize.

00:21:06.250 --> 00:21:10.220
Just what Google did to Link's photos.

00:21:10.220 --> 00:21:12.063
You can saturate these.

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:14.490
That's actually the point.

00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:19.380
To your own liking, you're
in complete control.

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:20.560
A lot of hidden gems in there.

00:21:20.560 --> 00:21:21.763
A lot of pages.

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:25.942
Went through a lot of
that, had a lot of notes.

00:21:25.942 --> 00:21:26.960
You know me.

00:21:26.960 --> 00:21:28.900
I like to give a lot of
notes on illustrations

00:21:28.900 --> 00:21:31.460
that involve us and our characters

00:21:31.460 --> 00:21:35.763
and our mythical crew and
our past and our future.

00:21:36.760 --> 00:21:38.040
Mythical.com.

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:39.630
Grab yourself the one,

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:42.513
the only official mythical coloring book.

00:21:43.980 --> 00:21:44.813
Okay, let's start-

00:21:44.813 --> 00:21:46.039
What you wanna do?

00:21:46.039 --> 00:21:49.563
With a question from Kanes Cab Driver,

00:21:51.884 --> 00:21:52.884
BudIceYall.

00:21:55.390 --> 00:21:56.810
BudIceYall.

00:21:56.810 --> 00:22:00.700
What's the proper amount
of time to honk at somebody

00:22:00.700 --> 00:22:03.660
when the light turns
green and they don't go?

00:22:03.660 --> 00:22:05.470
I give them a five second courtesy,

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:07.070
but my wife gives them three seconds.

00:22:07.070 --> 00:22:09.053
Oh, they're both timey.

00:22:09.920 --> 00:22:14.440
Now, I can't say that I
have an immediate answer.

00:22:14.440 --> 00:22:16.467
I'm gonna have to arrive at something

00:22:16.467 --> 00:22:20.690
because they've talked about
it and are in a constant count.

00:22:20.690 --> 00:22:22.110
I just can't live that way.

00:22:22.110 --> 00:22:24.387
I go on feel, I go on feel.

00:22:24.387 --> 00:22:25.220
You go on feel.

00:22:25.220 --> 00:22:30.220
